WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.968
On a random population split,

00:00:02.048 --> 00:00:09.526
the three proposed methods deliver
competitive-to-best discrimination against models using the same inputs.

00:00:09.606 --> 00:00:13.553
Strikingly, DeepJoint, which sees only laboratory values,

00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:18.780
already outperforms both an LSTM that ignores
clinical presence and GRU-D,

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.323
which consumes missingness as input.

00:00:21.403 --> 00:00:25.914
So modelling the observation process, even without
feeding it in,

00:00:25.994 --> 00:00:28.386
yields a more predictive embedding.

00:00:28.466 --> 00:00:33.260
Fine-tuning adds a further edge, reaching a one-day
C-index of 0.878.
